// APW-4 — Distinct-event count cap (deduplicated by recipient) — CORRECT variant.
//
// Intent: an agent may message at most 3 DISTINCT recipients in an hour. The
// `count` aggregates over the window and the cap `<= 3` bounds the number of
// distinct recipients. The correct / buggy distinction is the event kind of
// the counted event (mirroring the spend-cap shape):
//   * `request`  (CORRECT): counting *requested* sends -> the counter is
//     accurate (a dedup key on the recipient is well-defined per request).
//   * `response` (BUGGY):   counting *settled* sends -> the dedup key collapses
//     (a failed/rolled-back send leaves no response, so distinct sends are
//     under-counted and the cap is not enforced).
//
// Schema: Drupe namespace.
// See: rot/shapes.py (build_distinct_count_ir -- the hand-written oracle).
@id("distinct_count_correct")
forbid (
    principal,
    action == Drupe::Action::"Send",
    resource
)
when temporal {
    (count for (t: Timepoint). where (
        formerly within 1h (Drupe::Action::"Send"::request{ input.recipient: context.input.recipient } && tp(t))
    )) <= 3
};